\ render_zp.6502 - the renderer's save and restore of the game's zero page (src/render.6502
\ calls them). In sideways bank 4 below &9000, under ANDY: they run with ROMSEL &04 only (at the
\ start of render, before the movers go on, and at its end, after), which leaves room above
\ &9000 for the player's compiled kinds' table and code (step 2 layer 4).

\ ---- the game's zero page ----------------------------------------------------------------
\ The plotter's scratch bytes are also the logic's variables (delta_high is frame_and_flip,
\ screen_address is threshold...), and the original's logic reads, at the start of a pass, what
\ its own last drawing left there. So what the renderer does to the bytes the logic reads is
\ undone. Layer 3 (option B) keeps only those: the bytes whose first access by the logic after
\ a render was ever a read (tools/zplive.mjs, 2026-10-16, jsbeeb 2.5.0: four seeds, 30,000
\ frames each, the same 59 or 60, of which 13 the renderer's own work changes), less the
\ sprite unpacker's code at &04-&1E (the renderer never writes it), the MOS's (&E7-&ED), and
\ what the vsync interrupt counts meanwhile (field_count &90, game_over_cooldown &96); plus
\ the rest of &B0-&BB and &F8/&F9 (the plotter's leftovers) for margin. Pass lockstep proves it.
\ Decision 32: kept packed, the n-th byte saved at zp_save + n (34 bytes), so the rest of zp_save's
\ page holds the renderer's variables (src/render_bss.6502). A byte added here goes on the end.
.save_game_zp
    LDA &00
    STA zp_save + 0
    LDA &01
    STA zp_save + 1
    LDA &02
    STA zp_save + 2
    LDA &03
    STA zp_save + 3
    LDA &7E
    STA zp_save + 4
    LDA &7F
    STA zp_save + 5
    LDA &80
    STA zp_save + 6
    LDA &82
    STA zp_save + 7
    LDA &83
    STA zp_save + 8
    LDA &84
    STA zp_save + 9
    LDA &8E
    STA zp_save + 10
    LDA &8F
    STA zp_save + 11
    LDA &92
    STA zp_save + 12
    LDA &93
    STA zp_save + 13
    LDA &94
    STA zp_save + 14
    LDA &95
    STA zp_save + 15
    LDA &9B
    STA zp_save + 16
    LDA &9F
    STA zp_save + 17
    LDA &A0
    STA zp_save + 18
    LDA &B0
    STA zp_save + 19
    LDA &B1
    STA zp_save + 20
    LDA &B2
    STA zp_save + 21
    LDA &B3
    STA zp_save + 22
    LDA &B4
    STA zp_save + 23
    LDA &B5
    STA zp_save + 24
    LDA &B6
    STA zp_save + 25
    LDA &B7
    STA zp_save + 26
    LDA &B8
    STA zp_save + 27
    LDA &B9
    STA zp_save + 28
    LDA &BA
    STA zp_save + 29
    LDA &BB
    STA zp_save + 30
    LDA &C0
    STA zp_save + 31
    LDA &F8
    STA zp_save + 32
    LDA &F9
    STA zp_save + 33
    RTS

.restore_game_zp
    LDA zp_save + 0
    STA &00
    LDA zp_save + 1
    STA &01
    LDA zp_save + 2
    STA &02
    LDA zp_save + 3
    STA &03
    LDA zp_save + 4
    STA &7E
    LDA zp_save + 5
    STA &7F
    LDA zp_save + 6
    STA &80
    LDA zp_save + 7
    STA &82
    LDA zp_save + 8
    STA &83
    LDA zp_save + 9
    STA &84
    LDA zp_save + 10
    STA &8E
    LDA zp_save + 11
    STA &8F
    LDA zp_save + 12
    STA &92
    LDA zp_save + 13
    STA &93
    LDA zp_save + 14
    STA &94
    LDA zp_save + 15
    STA &95
    LDA zp_save + 16
    STA &9B
    LDA zp_save + 17
    STA &9F
    LDA zp_save + 18
    STA &A0
    LDA zp_save + 19
    STA &B0
    LDA zp_save + 20
    STA &B1
    LDA zp_save + 21
    STA &B2
    LDA zp_save + 22
    STA &B3
    LDA zp_save + 23
    STA &B4
    LDA zp_save + 24
    STA &B5
    LDA zp_save + 25
    STA &B6
    LDA zp_save + 26
    STA &B7
    LDA zp_save + 27
    STA &B8
    LDA zp_save + 28
    STA &B9
    LDA zp_save + 29
    STA &BA
    LDA zp_save + 30
    STA &BB
    LDA zp_save + 31
    STA &C0
    LDA zp_save + 32
    STA &F8
    LDA zp_save + 33
    STA &F9
    RTS

